<ol>
  <li>Open a shift on the till and count the cash in the drawer.</li>
  <li>Scan barcodes, or type part of a name or SKU and pick the product. Change the quantity for loose goods: 2.5 metres, 0.75 kg.</li>
  <li>Choose a customer if the sale goes on their account or needs their KRA PIN on the receipt.</li>
  <li>Take payment: cash (the till works out the change), M-Pesa, card, or a mix of them. On account for approved customers.</li>
  <li>The receipt prints. KRA's signed copy is added to it when eTIMS is connected.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Holding a sale</h2>
<p>If a customer goes to fetch something, <strong>Hold</strong> the sale and serve the next person. Held sales wait on the till until you bring them back.</p>

<h2>Returns and voids</h2>
<p>Find the sale under <strong>Sales</strong>, then <strong>Return items</strong> to refund part or all of it, putting the goods back into stock or not. A manager can void a sale made in error the same day.</p>

<h2>Closing the shift</h2>
<p>At the end of the day, count the drawer and close the shift. HardPoint shows what was expected and any difference, and prints the Z report.</p>
